None.   The  whole point of a traditional cpp is that it reflects
practices in pre‐standardization implementations of C.  Some  in‐
formation  is  available  from the first edition of Kernighan and
Ritchie.  Much of the rest of the  behavior  is  based  on  lore,
pragmatism,  material  encountered in the wild, and comparison to
other implementations.  The original version of was  written  one
